For any $ M, N \in S $,

$ f(N) - f(M) \in [\min f(P) - \max f(P),\ \max f(P) - \min f(P)] $

But:

- $ \min (f(N) - f(M)) = \min f(N) - \max f(M) $
- $ \max (f(N) - f(M)) = \max f(N) - \min f(M) $

But $ \min f(N) \ge \min f(P) $, and $ \max f(M) \le \max f(P) $

