Problem: In triangle \( ABC \), angle \( B \) is equal to \( 20^\circ \), angle \( C \) is equal to \( 40^\circ \). The length of the angle bisector \( AD \) is 2. Find the difference between the lengths of sides \( BC \) and \( AB \).

